            "question": "What pool fence height does South Carolina require?",
            "answer": "<p>South Carolina applies the International Swimming Pool and Spa Code with its 2021 building codes, and section 305 sets a 48-inch barrier. Our 46-inch tempered panel installed in spigots gives a 48-inch railing, so that is the pool panel for South Carolina. Add gate hinges and a latch for the opening, and ask your local building department about self-closing gate details before ordering.</p>",
